  "term": "ARI",
  "definition": "ARI refers to a norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor: a substance that blocks the return of norepinephrine, and sometimes epinephrine, into presynaptic nerve cells. This leaves more of the chemical in the synapse and increases adrenergic signaling.",
